# Seal access ledger — one line per sealed-split evaluation, ever.
# Committed on purpose: peeking at the held-out set is what destroys it, so
# every peek is permanent and public. A high ordinal means the sealed number
# has been iterated against and is no longer held out in any meaningful sense.
# `ordinal` is this file's own line number among non-comment lines, which is how
# scripts/bench.ts:appendSealLedger assigns it. `kind` says what a line is:
# absent means a sealed-split evaluation (every line up to 5), "preregistration"
# means a design registered BEFORE it was run, and "run" means that design's
# result. So the count of sealed peeks is the lines WITHOUT a kind, not the
# highest ordinal — and a pre-registration is committed before it can be edited
# by what the run found.
