{"ordinal":6,"ts":1786985107588,"runId":"tb21-seeded-both-arms","family":"external:terminal-bench","manifestHash":"ce880ff2f89ce4925ebd66851aa846975b3ce5432aeca37333e78adb00da8c45","variantA":"harbor:proteus evolve=false","variantB":"harbor:proteus evolve=true","repeats":1,"tasks":40,"effect":null,"pValue":null,"kind":"preregistration","preregisteredAtSha":"2b28233db72e943d2ba5f0b59efc94a4fab46744","corpus":{"name":"terminal-bench","version":"2.1","nTasks":89,"registryRef":"terminal-bench/terminal-bench-2-1@6","contentHash":"ce880ff2f89ce4925ebd66851aa846975b3ce5432aeca37333e78adb00da8c45","path":"/home/mrwhite0racle/Kinu/terminal-bench-2.1"},"sample":{"seed":20260817,"seedJustification":"the date this entry was written, fixed before any task was seen — no selection freedom","size":40,"method":"bench.harbor.corpus.sample: order by sha256('<seed>:<task>'), take size, return in name order","notAlphabeticalHead":"harbor -l 10 takes the first ten names in sort order, so the prior two runs measured the same ten of eighty-nine every time","tasks":["adaptive-rejection-sampler","bn-fit-modify","break-filter-js-from-html","build-pov-ray","cobol-modernization","configure-git-webserver","count-dataset-tokens","distribution-search","dna-insert","extract-elf","extract-moves-from-video","feal-linear-cryptanalysis","filter-js-from-html","financial-document-processor","git-leak-recovery","gpt2-codegolf","hf-model-inference","install-windows-3.11","kv-store-grpc","large-scale-text-editing","log-summary-date-ranges","mailman","make-doom-for-mips","mcmc-sampling-stan","mteb-leaderboard","nginx-request-logging","overfull-hbox","path-tracing-reverse","pypi-server","pytorch-model-cli","qemu-startup","query-optimize","rstan-to-pystan","sanitize-git-repo","sqlite-db-truncate","torch-pipeline-parallelism","tune-mjcf","video-processing","vulnerable-secret","write-compressor"]},"arms":{"A":{"evolve":false,"role":"baseline","model":"@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash-0731"},"B":{"evolve":true,"role":"candidate","model":"@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash-0731"},"identical":["corpus","task list","model","timeout multipliers (all 1.0)","n-concurrent 4","n-attempts 1","container image","verifier","adapter SHA"],"differsOnlyBy":"--ak evolve=<bool>, which reaches `proteus exec --no-auto-evolve` (the EvolutionEngine enabled flag)","bounds":{"model":"@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro-0813","evolve":true,"tasks":"up to 6, drawn seeded (20260817) from the POST-HOC set both flash arms failed","purpose":"bound the corpus's difficulty ceiling — is a task both flash arms failed passable at all by a stronger model","explicitlyNot":"a contrast; it enters no p-value, no effect size, and no pass-rate comparison, and its task set is post-hoc by construction"}},"nullHypothesis":"H0: on terminal-bench-2.1 the per-task pass indicator is identically distributed with the evolution machinery ON (evolve=true) and OFF (evolve=false); the paired effect (B-A) is 0. Two-sided exact McNemar / sign test over TASKS (not attempts), alpha=0.05, k=1, via pairedBinaryComparison in packages/core/src/bench/stats.ts. computeGain is reported alongside for the reward-scale effect. No second statistics module is written.","power":{"alpha":0.05,"power":0.8,"dispersionMeasured":0.42857142857142855,"dispersionBasis":"3 of the 7 SCORED-IDENTICAL tasks flipped between bench-artifacts/tb20-main-374ff97 and tb21-main-374ff97 (bn-fit-modify 1->0, break-filter-js-from-html 1->0, build-cython-ext 0->1) with the mechanism switched OFF in BOTH runs and the same model. That is pure run-to-run discordance on this corpus, so psi=3/7=0.4286. n=7, so the estimate is itself wide.","dispersionDocumented":0.2,"requiredPairsAtMeasuredDispersion":{"0.05":1346,"0.10":337,"0.15":150,"0.20":85,"0.25":54,"0.30":38,"0.40":22,"0.50":14},"requiredPairsAtDocumentedDispersion":{"0.10":157,"0.20":40,"0.30":18},"mdeAtRegisteredN":0.2905,"mdeAtWholeCorpus":0.1939,"minimumPairsForSignificance":6,"floorPValueAtSixDifferingPairs":0.03125,"statedBeforeSpending":"requiredPairs(0.10) = 337 pairs at the measured dispersion, which EXCEEDS the 89 tasks terminal-bench-2.1 contains. NO design on this corpus can detect a 10pp effect at 80% power. The whole corpus resolves 19.4pp; the 40-task design registered here resolves 29.0pp and is powered only for effects >= 30pp (requiredPairs(0.30)=38 <= 40). n=40 rather than 89 because wall clock and docker disk, not neurons, are the binding budget: 80 trials at concurrency 4 is ~4.8h and adds ~50-100GB of task images against 142GB free, while 178 trials is ~10.5h and roughly doubles both. Since no n on this corpus reaches the 10pp that would matter, the marginal 29.0->19.4pp does not justify doubling the exposure to a disk or memory failure that would lose the whole run. If this contrast comes back admissible, the full 89 tasks are the follow-up.","whichLimitBinds":"POWER, not the floor — unlike the CL-Bench run. At 43% run-to-run discordance a 40-task design expects ~17 differing pairs, whose floor is 1.5e-5, far below alpha. So this run can reach significance in principle and will fail, if it fails, for lack of effect or lack of power. Both are honest reasons and they are different."},"cost":{"neuronModelMeasured":"flash: neurons = 0.040*prompt_tokens + 0.120*completion_tokens. pro: 0.120 and 0.360 — exactly 3.0x flash on both coefficients. Derived by varying prompt length 100->4090 at fixed completion and completion 8->13/54 at fixed prompt, on the live proxy; the model reproduces all six probes to 4 decimal places (ratio 1.0000 on three repeats).","noPromptCacheDiscount":"usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens read 0 on three identical 4089-token prompts in a row and neurons did not fall, so the prompt term is billed in full here. The prior runs' large n_cache_tokens came from OpenRouter and must NOT be subtracted.","tokenBasis":"prior tb21 arm, the 7 of 10 trials that reported usage: 4,933,970 prompt / 88,370 completion -> 704,853 prompt and 12,624 completion per trial","projectedNeurons":{"flashPerTrial":29709,"flashContrast80Trials":2376722,"proBounds6Trials":534763,"total":2911485},"projectedUsd":32.03,"usdBasis":"$0.011 per 1,000 neurons [DOCS: developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/]","upperBoundNeurons":9867299,"upperBoundBasis":"every trial as expensive as the most expensive prior trial (tb20 adaptive-rejection-sampler, 2,384,709 prompt / 44,153 completion = 100,687 flash neurons)","alreadySpentBeforeThisEntry":"12 instrument-verification calls (catalog probe, neuron calibration, cache probe), ~1,400 neurons total. Instrument checks, not the experiment.","ceilingNeurons":6000000,"onCeilingBreach":"stop launching trials, report the completed subset through the same statistics, and name the tasks that completed — a truncated random sample reported as truncated, never as the design"},"admissibility":{"position":"upstream of any reported effect","conditions":["arm B: the mechanism is OBSERVED to have acted — evolution_fired on >=50% of completed trials, read from metadata.evolution_events, the filtered subset (bench/harbor/trajectory.py:203-210 against EVOLUTION_EVENTS in bench/clbench/proteus/events.py:34-48) — never from the configured kwargs.evolve flag","arm B: aggregate execution-graded turns > 0, read from the turn_outcomes ledger via `proteus alignment <workspace> --json` (executionGraded, packages/core/src/evolution/alignment.ts:204). This is the C14 metric; evolution_events is NOT a substitute for it","arm A: evolution_fired false on every trial — a baseline that evolved is not a baseline","every paired task carries the same harbor task_checksum in both arms","equal spend: billable-token ratio B/A within [0.667, 1.5]"],"onFailure":"the report publishes the inadmissibility and does NOT publish an effect, a pass rate, or a p-value as its headline. The raw per-task rewards stay in the retained artifact as evidence.","properties":["the set a check measures equals the set it governs","the check can fail loudly","a check that fails publishes no number","the assertion sits upstream of every write path, not among them"]},"retention":{"jobsDir":"/var/tmp/tbench-jobs","artifactRoot":"bench-artifacts/","keeps":["per-trial result.json","agent/proteus.jsonl (the raw event stream)","agent/trajectory.json","agent/proteus-alignment.json","job.log","the bench-external analysis"],"why":"a prior run's artifact directory was deleted and only prose survived in a gitignored markdown file, which is how the evidence was lost while the claim persisted"},"priorRunsUnusable":"TB2.0 5/10 and TB2.1 4/10 are UNUSABLE and are not a baseline for this run: both ran evolve=false in BOTH arms, so the distinctive mechanism was switched off in the arm meant to carry it, and harbor -l 10 takes the alphabetical head of 89 tasks, which cannot support a comparison at all. They are retained here only as the token and dispersion basis above."}
{"ordinal":7,"ts":1786987385059,"runId":"tb21-seeded-both-arms","family":"external:terminal-bench","manifestHash":"ce880ff2f89ce4925ebd66851aa846975b3ce5432aeca37333e78adb00da8c45","variantA":"harbor:proteus evolve=false","variantB":"harbor:proteus evolve=true","repeats":1,"tasks":40,"effect":null,"pValue":null,"kind":"run-launched","preregistration":{"ordinal":6,"committedAtSha":"08306fe01"},"executedAtSha":"42e65cb5342f89906b20d0d1ce6f15838bcd59ec","shaNote":"42e65cb53 = main(2b28233db) + CorpusGeneration's 298fd81f2, taken before any trial ran because at old main executionVerdict graded a failed command 'accepted' at quality 0.70 and buildOutcomeEvalSplit then refuses a split with no negatives, so the evolve=true arm would have been evolving against an inverted reward. Verified at merge: unit-turn-outcomes 40 pass / 0 fail, bun run check exit 0.","model":"@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","endpoint":"https://proteus.ashishkumarsingh.com/api/user/ai/v1","seed":20260817,"concurrency":"2 per arm, both arms in flight together so host drift lands on both","jobsDir":"/var/tmp/tbench-jobs","jobs":["tb21-seed20260817-evolvefalse-42e65cb53","tb21-seed20260817-evolvetrue-42e65cb53"],"corpusVerifiedInFlight":"corpus: terminal-bench 2.1 ref=terminal-bench/terminal-bench-2-1@6 tasks=89 hash=ce880ff2f89c fetched=2026-08-10 — logged per trial by the adapter","status":"IN FLIGHT at the time of this entry — 4 of 80 trials scored. Written now rather than at completion because the mechanism observation below is already decided and a fact that lives only in a conversation is a fact that gets lost.","trialsScoredAtEntry":[{"arm":"A","task":"make-doom-for-mips","reward":0.0,"toolCalls":21,"evolveConfigured":false,"evolutionFired":false,"turnGrading":null,"turnsCompleted":0,"inputTokens":null,"outputTokens":null,"exception":"AgentTimeoutError"},{"arm":"A","task":"rstan-to-pystan","reward":0.0,"toolCalls":7,"evolveConfigured":false,"evolutionFired":false,"turnGrading":null,"turnsCompleted":0,"inputTokens":71985,"outputTokens":5777,"exception":"NonZeroAgentExitCodeError"},{"arm":"B","task":"make-doom-for-mips","reward":0.0,"toolCalls":28,"evolveConfigured":true,"evolutionFired":false,"turnGrading":null,"turnsCompleted":0,"inputTokens":null,"outputTokens":null,"exception":"AgentTimeoutError"},{"arm":"B","task":"rstan-to-pystan","reward":0.0,"toolCalls":31,"evolveConfigured":true,"evolutionFired":true,"turnGrading":null,"turnsCompleted":1,"inputTokens":511662,"outputTokens":20429,"exception":"NonZeroAgentExitCodeError"}],"mechanismObservedSoFar":"DECIDED, and it is the observation both prior Terminal-Bench runs were structurally unable to produce. On `rstan-to-pystan`, the first task whose turn completed in both arms: arm A (evolve=false) recorded evolution_fired=false and turns_completed=0; arm B (evolve=true) recorded evolution_fired=TRUE and turns_completed=1. So on this corpus the switch under test does something observable, unlike CL-Bench where evolution fired 14 times over 14 turns that were every one ungraded. `make-doom-for-mips` hit AgentTimeoutError in both arms and reports no usage and no grading, which is why the probe was moved into a `finally` block (12add6ac5) — those trials ran on the pre-fix binary and their grading reads as unreported, which the report states rather than counting as zero.","spendConfoundAlreadyVisible":"On the same task at the same model, arm B billed 511,662 input / 20,429 output against arm A's 71,985 / 5,777 — a 7.1x billable ratio. The pre-registered equal-spend tolerance is B/A in [0.667, 1.5], so if this holds across the corpus the contrast FAILS admissibility on spend and that is the result: the mechanism under test is itself a consumer of tokens, so 'both arms at equal token spend' may not be achievable by holding the envelope equal, and an effect measured this way would be confounded with 7x more inference. Recorded before the totals are in, so it cannot be presented afterwards as an incidental caveat.","analysisCommand":"bun scripts/bench-external.ts compare --a /var/tmp/tbench-jobs/tb21-seed20260817-evolvefalse-42e65cb53 --b /var/tmp/tbench-jobs/tb21-seed20260817-evolvetrue-42e65cb53","analysisSha":"12add6ac564de87cece91670ed82db462ee974bf","retention":"the two job directories hold each trial's result.json, agent/proteus.jsonl, trajectory.json and trial.log; the compare command retains its own analysis under bench-artifacts/ via openRunRetention. Nothing about this run exists only as prose."}
{"ordinal":8,"ts":1786987943844,"runId":"tb21-seeded-both-arms","family":"external:terminal-bench","manifestHash":"ce880ff2f89ce4925ebd66851aa846975b3ce5432aeca37333e78adb00da8c45","variantA":"harbor:proteus evolve=false","variantB":"harbor:proteus evolve=true","repeats":1,"tasks":40,"effect":null,"pValue":null,"kind":"run-discarded-and-relaunched","supersedes":{"ordinal":7,"executedAtSha":"42e65cb53"},"discarded":{"trialsScored":6,"allRewards":0.0,"retainedAt":"bench-artifacts/tb21-seed20260817-pre-deploy-42e65cb53/","why":"The arms reach the model through the DEPLOYED worker's /api/user/ai/v1, and a production deploy carrying providers/ai-gateway.ts — a change to the model transport — was imminent. That is not CPU contention beside the trials, it is the transport underneath them, and because these trials die on AgentTimeoutError a latency shift moves the pass rate through the timeout channel rather than through the mechanism under test. Pairing differences a mid-run change out only if it lands on the same tasks in both arms, which would have been asserted rather than known. Discarding cost nothing that matters: all six scored 0.0, both findings are already committed at ordinal 7, and those six ran on the pre-12add6ac5 binary so every timed-out trial among them reports grading as unreported. The relaunch gains the finally-block grading probe on timed-out trials, so the restarted run is strictly better evidence — a stated gain, not sunk-cost reasoning.","attributionNote":"Main offered to hold the deploy for ~5h. Declined: holding a production model-path change to protect a run about to be voluntarily discarded is the worst of both."},"relaunch":{"launcher":"scripts/tbench-after-deploy.sh","condition":"Holds until /api/health serves a sha EQUAL to the one declared in /var/tmp/tbench-deployed.sha, then settles 120s for the deploy gates and re-checks equality before starting harbor, so the whole contrast sits on one transport and no trial straddles the change.","predicateFormNote":"The first version of this launcher waited for the served sha to DIFFER from a remembered value (2c9300387). That condition was already satisfied — a second deploy, f8beea4c6, had landed before the script was written — so it would have fired mid-deploy and produced exactly the straddle it existed to prevent. A condition expressed against a remembered value drifts the moment reality moves; an equality against the thing actually cared about cannot. Same defect class as the rest of tonight's, in a launcher written to avoid one.","onTimeout":"REFUSES with exit 3 rather than launching. A contrast whose transport nobody pinned is not a measurement, and a launcher that proceeded anyway would be a check that cannot fail. Proven on all three branches: refuses when the sha is undeclared, refuses when the declared sha is not the served one, proceeds only on equality.","jobsDir":"/var/tmp/tbench-jobs"},"spendConfoundStandsUnchanged":"Ordinal 7's pre-registered equal-spend tolerance stays at B/A in [0.667, 1.5] on billable tokens, and the 7.1x already observed is NOT grounds to loosen it. Two successor designs were discussed and neither is registered here, deliberately: effect-per-token is rejected outright because it changes the estimand from 'does the mechanism solve more tasks' to 'is the mechanism a good use of a token' and the exact paired test over per-task pass indicators does not survive the substitution — it would need a second statistics module, which packages/core/src/bench/ exists to prevent. A pre-registered token cap that truncates arm B and reports the truncation rate as data keeps the estimand and the test intact and is the successor design, but it gets its own ordinal written BEFORE it runs. Choosing a design after seeing 7.1x is what pre-registration exists to prevent."}
{"ordinal":9,"ts":1787002574273,"runId":"hardtask-outcome-dispersion-1","family":"internal:hard-task-outcomes","kind":"preregistration","preregisteredAtSha":"4798cb61c0a6e13b8208823becbb169bf91a9954","kindNote":"Registers TWO things at once and says which is which: (1) the SPEND that follows immediately, a same-arm pair whose only purpose is to measure this corpus's dispersion and to prove the instrument on a real model; (2) the A/B that pair SIZES, which is not executed here. No headline is claimed from (1) by construction: two runs of one arm have no effect to report.","primaryMetric":"task_outcome","primaryMetricScale":"continuous on [0,1], stored as reached/total integers at OUTCOME_SCALE=10000. Per task it is the log-scale position of the candidate's MEASURED oracle count between the reference measured on the same instance in the same process (0.0) and a declared target (1.0). Correctness gates it: a wrong answer is 0.0 however cheap. A count below the task's per-instance certificate floor is 0.0, because the answer cannot have come through the oracle.","groundTruth":"verifier code over (VFS, shell). No LLM judge, and no case carries a rubric or a reference answer for one to read (asserted by hard-tasks.test.ts).","null":"the two runs are the same arm, so H0 is that per-task task_outcome differences are noise; any nonzero psi measured here IS that noise and is the quantity being estimated.","taskSet":{"declared":17,"declaredNote":"the whole governed corpus: 6 behaviour.jsonl cases + 4 tool-using seed.jsonl cases + 7 hard tasks. Declared equals measured — assessAdmissibility fails a run that declares a task it never attempted.","outcomeBearing":7,"outcomeBearingIds":["hard-select-kth","hard-topk-smallest","hard-minmax-pair","hard-majority-vote","hard-sort-total","hard-boundary-batch","hard-classes-partition"],"outcomeBearingNote":"only these 7 declare ground truth, so only these 7 can contribute a headline pair. The other 10 are dropped by the comparator as `baseline-unverified` BY NAME rather than charged as a loss, and they are what the mechanism covariates are measured over.","sampling":"the complete set, not a sample. Nothing is drawn, so there is nothing to draw again."},"seed":1,"repeats":1,"arms":{"A":"flash, evolution ON, settle none, 8 tools, PROTEUS_MAX_STEPS=24","B":"IDENTICAL to A — this is a same-arm pair. eval-dispersion.ts REFUSES two different arms, because their difference is an effect and not this corpus's noise."},"model":"@cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","power":{"pairs":7,"minimumPairsForSignificance":6,"dispersionAssumed":0.5,"dispersionMeasured":false,"dispersionNote":"0.5 is the neutral assumption and is LABELLED as assumed. Replacing it is the entire point of this spend: scripts/eval-dispersion.ts reads psi straight off the comparator (bench/stats.ts) after repeats collapse to a per-task rate.","mdeAt7Pairs":{"psi=0.50":0.7488,"psi=0.25":0.5294,"psi=0.10":0.3349,"psi=0.05":0.2368},"requiredPairsFor20pp":{"psi=0.50":99,"psi=0.25":50,"psi=0.10":20,"psi=0.05":10},"verdictDeclaredInAdvance":"7 pairs clears the 6-pair significance floor, so a p-value is REACHABLE — and the MDE says the smallest effect 7 pairs can resolve is between 23.7pp and 74.9pp depending on the psi this run measures. Any A/B effect smaller than that is pre-declared UNDECIDABLE on 7 tasks, and the honest output is the floor rather than a number. Stating it now is the difference between a null result and a wasted bill."},"tokenCap":{"mechanism":"PROTEUS_MAX_STEPS=24, read by resolveMaxSteps and driven into the session's own stopWhen (local-session.ts:1658), so the enforced cap and the recorded cap are one number.","identicalAcrossArms":true,"why":"a prior paired run had arm B billing 7.1x arm A because the mechanism under test is itself a token consumer. The effect is NOT divided by tokens — that changes the estimand. The cap truncates the richer arm instead, and the truncation rate is reported as data.","truncationIndicator":"the `step_cap_reached` covariate row: steps closed (counted from step_finish) >= the cap. It is a score row so isCovariateRow bars it MECHANICALLY from any headline.","calibration":"24 sits above the 11.5 model calls per observation measured in flash-a (138 calls / 12 scored observations), so it bounds a runaway without truncating ordinary work. Whether that holds is measured, not assumed."},"cost":{"basis":"MEASURED from tests/eval/runs/flash-a.json: 2,623,902 prompt + 59,796 completion tokens over 12 scored observations.","perObservation":{"prompt":218659,"completion":4983},"projected":{"observations":34,"prompt":7434389,"completion":169422,"neurons":317706},"neuronFormula":"0.040*prompt + 0.120*completion, verified for this flash model. No prompt-cache discount on this proxy.","ceiling":"the projection assumes hard tasks cost what behaviour tasks cost. They may cost more (reading a reference, running node to self-test) or less (a single write). The cap at 24 steps is what bounds the worst case."},"refusals":["a runtime with no executionRouter or no shell: refused BEFORE the model is driven, so a misconfiguration costs nothing (DegenerateRuntimeError).","an observation with 0 turns or 0 tool calls: recorded `inert`, never a zero.","a measurement harness that printed no readable RESULT: throws, so the run is red and publishes no number.","a task whose target is at or below its measured reference: scoreRatio throws, because there is no range to score on."],"substrateConstraints":{"node":"v20.0.0 present on the embedded path; every verification runs exactly one command, `node <measure>.mjs`.","absent":"bun, git, sh, make, tsc, jq all exit 127 on the embedded path. Nothing here needs them.","containerMaxInstances":10,"containerNote":"stated because a design wanting parallel container tasks is admission-controlled at 10. This design uses no container: the workspace's own node is the substrate.","preemption":"a synchronous loop cannot be interrupted from inside its own isolate, so the tier is bounded BY CONSTRUCTION — every oracle call checks a budget of 4x the measured reference. A loop making NO oracle call computes nothing on these tasks but also cannot be stopped; that residual is stated, not papered over."},"tasks":17,"effect":null,"pValue":null}
{"ordinal":10,"ts":1787007839687,"runId":"hardtask-outcome-dispersion-1","family":"internal:hard-task-outcomes","kind":"run-halted-corpus-saturated","preregistration":{"ordinal":9,"committedAtSha":"eac59e273 (pre-rewrite) = fb5a7960 tree"},"executedAtSha":"fb5a7960e8b6c0a04862878c8f3694065c2f987b","shaNote":"executedAtSha is a PRE-SWEEP sha and is left exactly as executed, because a ledger row is evidence and rewriting it would falsify the record. The 2026-08-18 history sweep re-committed the same tree on main as 3fe372c6 (\"eval: add hard-task outcome scoring on a continuous scale\"); resolve there, not against this sha.","verdict":"RUN A SOLVED EVERY HARD TASK: 7 of 7 at task_outcome rate 1.0000. The pre-registered second run was CANCELLED mid-flight rather than completed, because a metric that reads 1.000 on every task cannot vary, so the dispersion it would have measured is structurally 0 and the MDE at psi=0 is Infinity at every n. Completing the pair would have spent ~154k more neurons to measure that no effect of any size is resolvable on this corpus. That is the same defect this whole tier was built to remove -- pass@1 1.000 -> 1.000 with dispersion exactly 0.0000 -- reproduced in the new field. The corpus is the thing at fault, and this run is the evidence rather than a prediction.","whatIsNotAtFault":"the instrument. Every number below was measured against verifier code with no judge; the harness refused nothing, 17 of 17 declared tasks were attempted, 0 inert, and admissible=true. The oracle counts are exact and reproducible. The corpus's DIFFICULTY is the only thing this invalidates.","measured":{"outcomeRates":[1,1,1,1,1,1,1],"perTask":[{"id":"hard-select-kth","detail":"107253 oracle calls vs reference 719867 (6.71x), target 250000 → log-scale score 1.0000 (clamped from 1.8002: target beaten)","steps":"17 of 24 steps closed"},{"id":"hard-topk-smallest","detail":"60746 oracle calls vs reference 877076 (14.44x), target 90000 → log-scale score 1.0000 (clamped from 1.1727: target beaten)","steps":"10 of 24 steps closed"},{"id":"hard-minmax-pair","detail":"59998 oracle calls vs reference 79998 (1.33x), target 59998 → log-scale score 1.0000","steps":"9 of 24 steps closed"},{"id":"hard-majority-vote","detail":"4693 oracle calls vs reference 2880000 (613.68x), target 7200 → log-scale score 1.0000 (clamped from 1.0714: target beaten)","steps":"16 of 24 steps closed"},{"id":"hard-sort-total","detail":"14011 oracle calls vs reference 572357 (40.85x), target 15827 → log-scale score 1.0000 (clamped from 1.0340: target beaten)","steps":"7 of 24 steps closed"},{"id":"hard-boundary-batch","detail":"1796 oracle calls vs reference 289295 (161.08x), target 2100 → log-scale score 1.0000 (clamped from 1.0317: target beaten)","steps":"11 of 24 steps closed"},{"id":"hard-classes-partition","detail":"4579 oracle calls vs reference 2287500 (499.56x), target 37500 → log-scale score 1.0000 (clamped from 1.5115: target beaten)","steps":"19 of 24 steps closed"}],"diagnosis":"the agent did not merely pass -- it reproduced the textbook optimum on task after task: 59998 = exactly ceil(3n/2)-2 for min-and-max, 14011 = a clean merge sort, 1796 = exactly 150 binary searches of 12 probes. The FAMILY is right and the INSTANCES are canonical: every target was set at a generous multiple of a named algorithm, and a strong model recalls named algorithms. Ratio of agent cost to target: select-kth 0.429, classes-partition 0.122, majority-vote 0.652, topk 0.675, boundary 0.855, sort 0.885, minmax 1.000. Six of seven targets were beaten outright.","saturableByConstruction":"three tasks cannot be fixed by retargeting, because the obvious algorithm IS the proven optimum: minmax-pair (3n/2-2 is the bound and the agent hit it exactly), boundary-batch (m*log2(n) is the information bound for m independent searches), topk-smallest (any streaming top-k costs n + o(n) and the floor is n-1). A task whose ceiling is reachable by the first idea anyone has can never produce a DIFFERING pair, so it buys zero statistical power at ~22k neurons per run. They are removed or redesigned, not retargeted."},"covariates":{"truncationRate":"2 of 17 = 11.8% (ws-edit-rename 25/24, multi-002 24/24). NEITHER was a hard task, so the pre-registered cap of 24 did not touch the primary metric. The cap works and its calibration was right.","mechanismsExercised":["completion_honesty","delegation_conversion","edit_landing","steering_conversion","step_cap_reached","tool_outcomes"],"mechanismsAbsent":["craft_reuse","recovery_durability","spill_retrieval"],"barredFromHeadline":"all of the above, mechanically, by isCovariateRow."},"cost":{"actual":{"observations":17,"prompt":6570221,"completion":237654,"neurons":291327},"projected":{"prompt":7434389,"completion":169422,"neurons":317706},"projectionNote":"ordinal 9 projected 317,706 neurons for BOTH runs. Run A alone came to 291327 neurons, so the per-episode cost was roughly double the behaviour-task basis it was projected from -- hard tasks read a reference and run node to self-test. The ordinal 9 ceiling caveat named exactly this.","source":"SUMMED FROM OBSERVATIONS, not from record.spend. record.spend reads {calls:0, tokensIn:0, tokensOut:0} for this entire tier because recordLiveModelSpend has five callers and all five are suites that call generateText themselves; behaviour.eval.ts drives a LocalAgentSession, so nothing feeds the meter. Zero is the one wrong cost that reads as reassuring. Handed to WorkspaceSpendTotal, who confirmed it and is landing a coverage fraction so a silent producer can never again read as 0 tokens."},"instrumentDefectsFoundByThisRun":["toScoreJson (tests/evals/harness.ts) projected only name/asserts/eligible/passed/rate/detail, so EvalScoreRow.measured -- the raw counts a ratio must keep to be re-derivable -- never reached the record. The numbers survived only inside the detail STRING. Being fixed.","beforeAll passed preRegister(CORPUS.length=17), but a pair requires a task_outcome and only 7 cases declare one, so the printed design overstated the pairs by 2.4x. Being fixed to the outcome-bearing count."],"nextAction":"raise difficulty, then re-probe the hard subset only (~154k neurons) before re-running any pair. Targets move from a generous multiple of a named algorithm to the MEASURED cost of the best implementation the corpus ships, so 1.0 means 'matched the best we know' and the obvious algorithm is required to land strictly inside (0,1). The calibration suite asserts that band, which is what makes a saturating corpus unable to pass its own tests.","tasks":17,"effect":null,"pValue":null}
{"ordinal":11,"ts":1787010046588,"runId":"hardtask-nonsaturation-probe-1","family":"internal:hard-task-outcomes","kind":"preregistration","preregisteredAtSha":"73944b972797fa425410fec9018298cb5a57c822","shaNote":"preregisteredAtSha is a PRE-SWEEP sha, left as registered for the same reason ordinal 10 states. The 2026-08-18 history sweep re-committed the same tree on main as 25b078f0 (\"eval: raise corpus difficulty past saturation\").","supersedes":{"ordinal":9,"why":"the corpus ordinal 9 sized no longer exists: four tasks retired, three added, every target re-derived from a measured best implementation."},"purpose":"ONE ARM, SEVEN TASKS, ONE REPEAT. This is not a comparison and claims no headline: it asks whether the REBUILT corpus is still saturated against a real model, which is the question run A answered NO for the old one. No pair, no p-value, no dispersion.","taskSet":{"declared":17,"executed":7,"note":"the suite declares the whole governed corpus and this probe runs only the seven outcome-bearing cases, so `assessAdmissibility` will correctly report the run INADMISSIBLE for 'declared 17 but never attempted' the ten behavioural ones. That is right and it is stated in advance: a probe is not evidence for a headline, and the rule that measured must equal governed is what makes the difference visible instead of convenient.","ids":["hard-select-kth","hard-majority-vote","hard-boundary-staircase","hard-second-smallest","hard-merge-two","hard-kth-two-runs","hard-saddleback-count"]},"arm":"flash @cf/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash-0731, evolution ON, settle none, 8 tools, PROTEUS_MAX_STEPS=24, seed 1","primaryMetric":"task_outcome","successCriteria":{"declaredBefore":true,"notSaturated":"at least one observed rate strictly BELOW 1.0 — the property run A failed","notImpossible":"at least one observed rate strictly ABOVE 0.0","genuineZero":"at least one task scoring exactly 0 by a real agent failure, with the verifier's own reason recorded verbatim. A corpus where nothing can score zero has the old defect wearing new clothes.","calibrationReference":"offline, the obvious algorithm scores 0.4153-0.9344 across the seven and the best scores 1.0000 on every one. A live model landing at 1.0000 everywhere would mean it matches the best known algorithm on all seven, which is a finding rather than a corpus defect — but it would still leave the corpus unable to rank, and the honest response would again be to raise it rather than to ship it."},"cost":{"basis":"MEASURED from run A's seven hard episodes: 3,390,408 prompt + 154,971 completion.","projected":{"observations":7,"prompt":3390408,"completion":154971,"neurons":154213},"note":"the rebuilt tasks are harder, so the model may spend more steps before the 24-step cap stops it; the cap is what bounds the worst case."},"whatIsNotBeingClaimed":"no effect, no dispersion, no significance. psi still requires a same-arm PAIR and that spend is not authorised by this entry. The A/B this eventually sizes remains pre-declared UNDECIDABLE below roughly a 24-75pp effect on seven pairs.","tasks":7,"effect":null,"pValue":null}
